{"kind":"report","text":"Approved lane F revision 3 at exact head a65b34f58e5b752c9430da54b4ac0a86319bd69a, resting on all 58 artifacts.\n\nBoth findings from review 88a20f74 are resolved. publication-unresolved descriptions now state only recorded readback facts. Recovery text comes from the loaded operation, shares recoveryNow with the landing cards, gives abort precedence even when token revocation failed, and marks the current state unknown when the operation was not loaded. Explain titles use the same rule. Whole compiled draft policies now pass through the runtime's validatePolicy before replay, with validation problems and a fix instead of predictions for invalid documents. All four draft kinds retain the validation boundary.\n\nIndependent validation: root strict typecheck passed; 88 UI component/adapter tests passed; all 6 Playwright browser tests passed, including the scenario, review submission and keyboard navigation. I reran the two original independent reproductions with the repaired expectations, additionally using an abort whose tokenRevoked is false: both passed, including all five invalid-draft cases. The phone capture now waits for the changed-file diff; the fresh 390×6842 image is byte-identical to the committed capture. Changed light/dark Room images and the complete phone Proposal image were visually inspected. The remaining unchanged artifacts carry the previous exact-head review evidence; all changed UI code, tests, README and capture logic were reviewed again. The merged policy-pack changes have their separately recorded approval and landed receipt.\n\nArchitecture: one adapter remains a useful boundary between mock and live Rooms. The shared recovery sentence eliminates divergence between feed, explanation and operation cards. Policy prediction uses the same document validator and evaluator as admission. Loaded operation facts and bounded read coverage preserve uncertainty honestly.\n\nSecurity: compromise aborts cannot accidentally be described as continuing forward, and an invalid policy cannot be presented as ready for adoption. The live adapter does not request or display workspace credentials. This approval does not claim a deployed live-client integration: diff, active policy, slot and other unavailable reads remain explicitly documented gaps until the integration contract supplies them.\n\nSimplification: the changes use two clear boundaries—whole-document validation before replay, and current recovery facts from a loaded operation—without adding a competing rules engine or endpoint. Plain-English refusals, recovery explanations, responsive layout and keyboard flow remain clear. No additional blocking finding in this revision.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9f9d9cfecbd2371b852b5fca99165b79ad404bad","binding":"assigned","head":"a65b34f58e5b752c9430da54b4ac0a86319bd69a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6b2af22c0fa327b20648dcdc6564405dde57efe0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:20cf77e0d8e8478ea9044953ed5903b698055dc1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6b2af22c0fa327b20648dcdc6564405dde57efe0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}